# ibl.ai configuration. NOTHING HERE IS REQUIRED, and nothing writes it.
#
# The app configures itself: open it and press Start. The platform goes into
# data/onboarding.db, and the agent and the app's name into the platform's own
# metadata, so a deployed app can still change them. Every key below has a
# default in lib/iblai/config.ts — this file is the list of knobs, not a setup
# step. Copy it to .env.local (gitignored) only if you need one of them.
#
# Nothing in it is a secret either: the app holds no platform API key. The
# buyer's own sign-in token and the admin's own sign-in token are the only
# credentials it ever sends; the Platform API Token lives in iblai.env, for
# deploying only.

# Self-hosting. The four platform URLs default to hosted iblai.app; set
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PLATFORM_BASE_DOMAIN to your own domain and, if each service has
# its own subdomain rather than one consolidated origin, leave
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL unset. The auth host is not derivable from the
# domain, so NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTH_URL is its own knob.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PLATFORM_BASE_DOMAIN=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTH_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_WS_URL=

# What the setup wizard answers, should you ever want to pin one by hand
# instead. The wizard skips whatever is already answered. The agent is the last
# path segment of its os.ibl.ai URL,
# https://os.ibl.ai/platform/<platform-key>/<agent-uuid>; the name is what the
# login screens, the browser tab and the Stripe product call the app
# (human-readable, two or three words in Title Case — Babatunde Tutor — never a
# slug).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MAIN_TENANT_KEY=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DEFAULT_AGENT_ID=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_NAME=

# What this app is called on the platform: it tags the Stripe product
# (metadata.app, which the platform's checkout enforces) and keys both the
# paywall choice and the wizard's answers in the platform's public metadata
# (apps.<slug>). You do not set this: the wizard mints one of its own from the
# app's name the first time it is set up — <name>_<uuid>, so two apps on one
# platform never collide — and stores it. This is only the fallback an app set
# up before that keeps using.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PAYWALL_APP_SLUG=vibe-agent

# Support address shown in the SDK's chat surfaces (defaults to support@ibl.ai).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPPORT_EMAIL=

# Mobile (Tauri iOS/Android) SSO return scheme. Desktop and web ignore it.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TAURI_CUSTOM_SCHEME=vibe-agent

# Show the About tab and /about (off by default).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SHOW_ABOUT=false
